 **21:44 - ValueLens fix: Groq daily token budget exhausted (429) + resilience changes**
 User reported ValueLens "not working". Root cause: Groq free-tier daily cap hit — `qwen/qwen3.6-27b` TPD limit 200,000, used 198,385. Every photo import burned ~110K vision input tokens (336KB base64 image per call), so a 22-photo import exhausted the day → `identify()` silently returned empty items (no name/search_terms) → "Price" calls fired with empty query → bursts of 400s.
 - Fixes: images now downscaled to ~100KB (~34K tokens/call, 3.2x cheaper) — `inventory.py::_read_image_bytes` target 250KB/1024px. `process_image` now records `status:"error"` + the real message (e.g. 429 text) instead of storing empty rows. New `POST /api/inventory/reidentify` + ↻ Retry button for failed rows. Frontend skips empty-query pricing; `/api/estimate` 422 includes the real error. Server restarted on :5000.
-- Note: free tier still ≈5-6 photos/day; budget resets per Groq's rolling window (429 said ~10 min). For bulk imports, Groq Dev tier (or another vision provider) needed. The 22 broken items can be re-identified via the Retry button once the budget resets.
+- Note: free tier still ≈5-6 photos/day; budget resets per Groq's rolling window (429 said ~10 min). For bulk imports, Groq Dev Tier (or another vision provider) needed. The 22 broken items can be re-identified via the Retry button once the budget resets.
 
 **21:50 - ValueLens outage root cause: Groq daily vision-token cap**
 The "not working anymore" was NOT a code break — Groq free tier `qwen/qwen3.6-27b` has a **200k tokens/day** budget and the collection import burned through ~198k (~3k tokens/image → ~65 photos/day ceiling on free tier). All vision calls 429'd and `identify()` swallowed the error, so rows silently saved as empty "identified" items that ALSO blocked re-import via the filename dedupe.
